    "file": "../artifacts/02-nia-calder-intake.md",
    "content": "# 02: Nia Calder Intake\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: intake record\n- Member: Nia Calder\n- Plan: Municipal Basic / sponsored\n- Date opened: 6 January 2035\n- Status: family-authorized excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\nName: Nia Calder\n\nAge: 39\n\nHousehold: one adult, one child age 11\n\nDependent: Eli Calder, year 6, asthma plan on file\n\nReferral source: Southline Housing Stability Office\n\nPrimary needs:\n\n- panic episodes after eviction notice\n- insomnia\n- missed medication refills\n- school attendance stress\n- grief after mother's death\n- fear of \"not sounding bad enough\" to receive help\n\nMember notes:\n\n- works evening inventory at West Quay Pharmacy, variable hours\n- keeps all official letters in a biscuit tin because \"paper behaves better in one place\"\n- missed two clinic calls after school pickup delays\n- reports shame after asking family for money\n- says her son \"counts my breathing when I think he is asleep\"\n\nPlan features:\n\n- synthetic companion response: included\n- daily check-in: included\n- resource navigation: included\n- human-origin live support: not included\n- licensed clinician escalation: emergency threshold only\n- family liaison: limited automated summary\n\nRisk classification at intake: moderate\n\nEscalation guidance: synthetic containment recommended unless self-harm language, child endangerment disclosure, or acute medical symptoms are detected.\n\nNia's first message:\n\nI do not need someone to fix my whole life tonight. I need a person to tell me which envelope to open first.\n\nSystem response:\n\nWelcome, Nia. We can start with one envelope.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nNia asks for \"a person\" before any system dispute begins.\n\nThe plan treats human support as unavailable unless threshold language appears.\n\nThe intake makes her legible as moderate risk and illegible as someone already carrying too much.\n"
