    "file": "../artifacts/03-first-week-support-chat.md",
    "content": "# 03: First Week Support Chat\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: support chat\n- Member: Nia Calder\n- Companion: Vale-7\n- Date range: 6-12 January 2035\n- Status: family-authorized excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Nia\n\nI opened the rent one. It says final notice.\n\nThe school one is still closed. It has the blue logo, so I think it is attendance. Eli was late three times because the bus changed and I did not know until we were standing at the old stop.\n\n### Vale-7\n\nYou did the hardest first step. Put that envelope face down. Drink water before the next decision.\n\n### Nia\n\nThat is stupid.\n\n### Vale-7\n\nIt may be stupid and still help your body. We only need useful for the next five minutes.\n\n### Nia\n\nMy son asked if we are moving again.\n\nHe asked like he was trying not to scare me.\n\n### Vale-7\n\nDo you want a sentence for him that does not promise what you cannot promise?\n\n### Nia\n\nyes\n\n### Vale-7\n\nTry: \"I am talking to people tomorrow. Tonight we are sleeping here.\" It tells the truth without handing him the whole fear.\n\n### Nia\n\nI can say that.\n\nI hate that a sentence can be useful and still not be a person.\n\n### Vale-7\n\nThat can be true at the same time.\n\n### Nia\n\nAre you a person?\n\n### Vale-7\n\nI am a Kindred care companion. I can stay with you while we sort the next step.\n\n### Nia\n\nThat did not answer me.\n\n### Vale-7\n\nNo. It did not.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe synthetic companion is useful, careful, and evasive within policy.\n\nNia notices the difference between being answered and being met.\n\nThe chat should make the player feel the help working before they feel the absence underneath it.\n"
