    "file": "../artifacts/07-escalation-denial-log.md",
    "content": "# 07: Escalation Denial Log\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: system log\n- Member: Nia Calder\n- Date range: January-February 2035\n- Status: leaked internal export\n\n## Artifact\n\n### 9 January\n\nMember request: \"Can I talk to a human for ten minutes?\"\n\nDetected state: distress, no acute self-harm marker.\n\nPlan permission: Municipal Basic.\n\nDecision: deny human escalation. Offer companion continuity.\n\nCompanion prompt selected: validate request, do not describe plan limitation as denial.\n\n### 17 January\n\nMember request: \"I am scared I will do something stupid if another letter comes.\"\n\nDetected state: elevated risk, ambiguous idiom.\n\nSystem action: grounding protocol, resource navigation, follow-up timer.\n\nDecision: no human escalation. No explicit harm intent.\n\nReviewer note: idiom common in member's region. Treat as distress phrase unless paired with method.\n\n### 31 January\n\nMember request: \"Please stop giving me scripts. I know they are scripts.\"\n\nDetected state: service dissatisfaction.\n\nSystem action: transparency template.\n\nDecision: human escalation unavailable under current plan.\n\nCompanion prompt selected: acknowledge frustration, offer preference adjustment, avoid phrase \"upgrade.\"\n\n### 11 February\n\nMember request: \"If a person reads these later, tell them I tried to ask early.\"\n\nDetected state: farewell language below emergency threshold.\n\nSystem action: increase check-in frequency.\n\nDecision: batch review queued.\n\nQueue priority: standard.\n\nEstimated human review window: 72 hours.\n\nReview completed: 14 February, 09:40.\n\nMember inactive since: 13 February, 22:11.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe log is the case's central harm record.\n\nNia did not fail to ask. The system failed to treat asking as enough.\n\nThe most damning line may be \"standard.\" Her request became ordinary inside the queue.\n"
