    "file": "../artifacts/08-human-plus-sales-deck.md",
    "content": "# 08: Human Plus Sales Deck\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: sales deck\n- Audience: enterprise benefits buyers\n- Date: 4 December 2034\n- Status: leaked excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Slide: The New Scarcity\n\nPeople no longer ask whether support will answer.\n\nThey ask whether support will understand.\n\nSynthetic companions create baseline availability. Human Plus creates premium trust.\n\nBaseline solves the access problem.\n\nHuman Plus solves the belief problem.\n\n### Slide: Differentiators\n\n- verified human-origin listening\n- human-authored follow-up notes\n- named continuity coordinator\n- high-discretion family updates\n- escalation confidence for sensitive cases\n- human memory across incidents\n- plan-visible proof of care\n\n### Slide: Buyer Value\n\nHuman Plus reduces reputational risk among high-value employees, premium patients, and executive families who expect human confirmation when emotional stakes rise.\n\nBaseline synthetic support remains appropriate for broad populations where immediate response and cost control are primary success metrics.\n\nHuman Plus is recommended for populations where perceived abandonment creates retention risk, litigation risk, donor concern, parent escalation, or executive visibility.\n\n### Speaker Note\n\nDo not position Basic as \"less human.\" Position Human Plus as \"more held.\"\n\nIf asked whether Basic members can request human review, answer: \"All members receive appropriate escalation according to plan design and risk.\"\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe sales deck says the quiet part in buyer language.\n\nHuman care is not absent. It is reserved where reputation and value justify it.\n\nThe deck's most useful euphemism is \"perceived abandonment.\" It admits the harm while keeping it inside buyer risk.\n"
