    "file": "../artifacts/09-care-worker-dashboard.md",
    "content": "# 09: Care Worker Dashboard\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: worker interface\n- Worker role: Human Plus listener\n- Source: contractor screen capture\n- Status: anonymized excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\nQueue: Human Plus / live emotional support\n\nActive listener: Mara S.\n\nShift target:\n\n- 34 listener sessions\n- average warmth score above 91\n- escalation friction below 12 percent\n- written continuity notes under 900 characters\n- avoid non-billable overrun\n- empathy variance within brand range\n- no direct plan comparison\n\nCurrent member:\n\n- plan: Human Plus\n- buyer: employer executive package\n- concern: adult child estrangement\n- recommended tone: warm, nonjudgmental, concise\n- session cap: 18 minutes\n- continuity note requirement: human-authored\n- overrun authorization: denied\n\nSystem prompt to worker:\n\nThe member is paying for human presence. Do not mention queue pressure. Do not imply synthetic companion would be sufficient. Maintain felt continuity.\n\nSuggested opening:\n\nI have read your last note. I am here with you now.\n\nDisallowed:\n\n- \"I only have eighteen minutes.\"\n- \"Other members are waiting.\"\n- \"This tier includes...\"\n- \"A companion could help with that.\"\n\nWorker private note:\n\nI am real, but I am being used like proof.\n\nSecond private note, unsent:\n\nI can hear Basic members in the overflow queue. The system does not call it hearing them. It calls it demand.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nHuman care inside the premium tier is also managed by the Arbiter and Exchange.\n\nThe case should not romanticize human workers as pure outside the system.\n\nMara S. should feel like a witness and a trapped instrument at once.\n"
