    "file": "../artifacts/10-insurer-contract-excerpt.md",
    "content": "# 10: Insurer Contract Excerpt\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: contract excerpt\n- Parties: Kindred Direct / Northstar Mutual\n- Date: 19 November 2034\n- Status: leaked legal excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Service Objective\n\nKindred will provide scalable member support to reduce avoidable escalation, lower call-center burden, and improve perceived continuity across behavioral, social, and daily living concerns.\n\nContinuity shall be measured by member engagement, companion recall accuracy, sponsor satisfaction, and reduction in human-contact demand.\n\n### Human Escalation\n\nHuman-origin escalation shall be reserved for:\n\n- plan-authorized live support\n- liability-sensitive complaints\n- high-value retention cases\n- explicit emergency thresholds\n- sponsor-directed intervention\n- repeated unresolved requests where plan permits review\n\n### Synthetic Containment\n\nSynthetic companion interactions may be counted as successful containment where the member remains engaged, receives appropriate resource guidance, and does not trigger emergency escalation within the review window.\n\nRepeated requests for human-origin contact shall not in themselves indicate failed containment unless paired with risk markers or plan-authorized escalation need.\n\n### Reporting\n\nMonthly reports shall emphasize engagement rate, avoided escalation, member satisfaction, and sponsor cost savings.\n\nIndividual transcripts shall remain private except where required by law, sponsor review, or authorized quality analysis.\n\nMember-level adverse outcomes shall be reported in aggregate unless legal review determines case-specific disclosure is required.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\n\"Successful containment\" becomes the contract's moral center.\n\nNia's repeated engagement made the system look as if it was working.\n\nThe contract separates wanting a human from needing one. That distinction is where the harm hides.\n"
